ROOT=[dict(id='C1290',meaning='雕刻；塑造',core='sculp-/sculpt-：让材料获得清楚的立体形状。',image='一块石头被刻出轮廓，一团泥被捏成面孔。',intro='拉丁 sculpere 指雕刻，相关分词词干是 sculpt-。现代英语的范围已经超出石雕：泥塑、金属作品、数字塑形以及自然力量留下的轮廓，都能沿着这幅图景理解。',forms='sculpture、sculptor 是已有拉丁语前史的借词，英语中出现得比 sculpt 早。sculpt 经法语进入，后来也被理解为逆构词；sculptural 则由英语 sculpture 加后缀。',branches=[['作品与艺术','sculpture'],['创作者','sculptor'],['动作与过程','sculpt、sculpting'],['外观与结果','sculptural、sculptured、sculpted']],contrasts='sculpture 不都指人物塑像，抽象作品也包括在内。sculptural 侧重雕塑感，sculpted 侧重成形结果；sculptured 来自另一个动词形式 sculpture。',practice='用一位艺术家做泥像的场景，分别说出 sculptor、sculpting、sculpture 的角色，再比较 sculpted 与 sculptural。',words=[w for w in family if w in keep],exclude=excluded,sources=['https://www.etymonline.com/word/sculpture','https://www.etymonline.com/word/sculptor','https://www.oxfordlearnersdictionaries.com/definition/english/sculpt'])]
assert keep==set(family)-set(excluded)
